{# The ORDER's own entry at the TOP of the shared bar's ⋯ overflow — the `overflowTemplate` slot
   `admin/_partials/sales_document_action_bar.html.twig` documents and no document filled before
   now. Expects: `document`, the SalesOrder; `isOrderLocked`, passed through `overflowContext` by
   `_tab_nav.html.twig`.

   Void was reachable only through the "Update Order Status" modal (detail.html.twig,
   summary_info_status / page_end blocks) — a `<select>` offering Approved and Void that posts XHR
   to this SAME `admin_order_update_status` route, the same verb, the same `status` value. This is
   that endpoint again, as a plain form so it works with scripting off, exactly the way Clone right
   below it already does.

   The guard is the modal's own trigger guard, word for word: `not isOrderLocked` (Closed or Void).
   OrderController::updateStatus() refuses BOTH Approve and Void once the order is in either state
   (isOrderLockedForEditing()), so this does not offer a control the route would only turn away —
   and it does not additionally ask `document_is_locked()` because the modal's trigger never did
   either; an explicitly locked-but-not-Closed-or-Void order still shows this button today the same
   way it still shows the modal's own pencil, and the route's own `assertWritable()` is what answers
   that case. #}
{% if not isOrderLocked %}
    <form id="order-action-void-form" method="post" action="{{ path('admin_order_update_status', {id: document.id}) }}" style="display: contents;">
        {{ csrf_field() }}
        <input type="hidden" name="status" value="Void">
        <button id="order-action-void" class="danger" type="submit">Void Order</button>
    </form>
{% endif %}
